  "description": "Global - International Ports is a dataset listed in energydata.info, an open data portal for energy in developing countries under the section \"Economics and prices\", published or maintained by World Bank Group. Ports were extracted from the UNCE global repository ( ), and were combined with port flows data from LPI logisitcs. All ports with reported international trade in Q1 of 2020 were attributed with the sum of Quarterly deployed capacity (TEU). Coverage: 187 countries in East Asia and the Pacific, Europe and Central Asia, the Middle East and North Africa, South Asia. It has 3 files in JSON, VECTOR API, ZIP. The portal files it under Economics and prices. The portal gives 2020 as the release date. It is reached through the links recorded on this page, with the catalogue entry as the discovery route. Access is free of charge and open. The licence is CC-BY-4.0. Caveats: this record was written from the catalogue listing only, so the linked page was not opened, its contents and current availability were not checked, and the description may lag the source. It can support power-system and electrification planning studies. Related record: the catalogue-level record data-energydata-info-world-bank.",
